Asgard was a Private Military company formed in 1986 by [[Emperor Mikael Khalindar IV]], it was designed to be a proxy force of the Empire of Khalindar<ref>This was debated by experts until the merging of Asgard into Khalindar and the collapse of the Empire of Khalindar in 1998</ref>. Asgard was capable of entering conflicts where the Empire of Khalindar's military was unable to go and bring nations into the Empire of Khalindar's sphere without a direct intervention on the Empire of Khalindar's part. Asgard was led by [[CEO Ødger Nyberg]] and consisted of the finest special forces operatives The Empire of Khalindar had to offer<ref>The members of Asgard consisted of operators from the Royal Khalindar Knights Service, Royal Khalindar Cobra Service, Royal Khalindar Maritime Interdiction Operation Service, Royal Khalindar Special Boat Service, and the Royal Khalindar Special Air Service</ref>.  Asgard's military operations would initially be headed by an unnamed Cobra force operator until 1994 when a veteran of the Avant world War by the name of  [[Bjorn Uskalai]]<ref>Bjorn Uskalai would become one of the major causes for The Empire of Khalindars downfall</ref> nicknamed Hogvakten while he was in Asgard would take over Asgard's military operations. Their military arsenals was provided by the Empire of Khalindar's funding and by a influential arms dealer who went by the name of [[Surtur]]. Surtur also operated as Asgard's 2nd in command.<ref>Surtur would find himself retiring after a debacle involving chemical weapons he bought from Zhensanov in  1996. Bjorn Uskalai would take over his position as 2nd in command shortly thereafter</ref> these 3 men combined would help to build Asgard into the influential and feared Military force that would become the fist of the Empire of Khalindar's clandestine operations around the world.
<references />Asgard's first combat operation would be at the Behest of the emperor, he would order them to intervene in the [[Khopda Taoist Revolutionary Revolt of 1987|'''Khopda Taoist Revolutionary Revolt of 1987''']].<ref>The first Taoist revolt in Khopda, it would be followed nearly a decade later by a second</ref> Their intervention in the Khopda Taoist revolutionary revolt would come to an abrupt end when the [[Avant World War]] kicked off in 1990.<ref>Asgards unfinished work would allow for a second taoist revolution in 1994</ref> The Emperor would directly call upon Asgard to engage in special operations. Asgard was specifically responsible for destroying Solaran supply lines and harassing  Solaran units throughout the war. Near the end of the conflict the current head of military operations would die leaving a vacancy that at the end of the war Bjorn Uskalai would fill, his experience in the Avant World War would make him a excellent choice for the position. Shortly after Asgard found itself a new head of combat operations Asgard would begin recruiting and rebuilding after the Avant World War, by the time they found themselves deploying in 1996 to the  [[Khopda Taoist Revolutionary Revolt of 1994|'''Khopda Taoist Revolutionary Revolt of 1994''']] on the Emperor's orders Asgard had managed to gather together 2000 elite operators. These operators would soon be joined by a further 2000 operators that were fired from the Empire of Khalindar's military service.<ref>Experts debate whether the sudden firing of 2000 operators was intentional however they would soon find out after those operators joined Asgard that it was most likely a ploy by the Emperor</ref> Those Operators would be split between Khopda and the [[1st Astorian Mariposan War]].<ref>Experts debate whether Asgards contributions were the deciding factors in both conflicts </ref> The conclusion of the 1st Astorian Mariposan war in 1997 would see Asgard shift the majority of its troops to fight in Khopda where Surtur had been controlling the frontline<ref>Aurendale military command holds the Belief that Surtur utilized chemicals weapons on the Aurendale foreign legion and Taoist rebels in the same strike, while nothing was proved relations between the 2 groups most definitely soured due to it.</ref>. Quick commands by Bjorn would push the Taoists into a corner, however once again before he could strike the finishing blow the [[2nd Astorian Mariposan War]] would kick off in late 1997 forcing Asgard to shift the majority of their troops once again over to fight in Mariposa.<ref>This conflict would prove to be particularly brutal for Asgard and would mark their final combat operation before their absorption into the Empire of Khalindar. </ref> After the conclusion of the 2nd War, Asgard would find itself absorbed into the empire of Khalindars military. This marked the end of Asgard as a private entity.

