== Prologue "A Wild World" ==
=== Introduction === "Book 0" in the Avant Garde Nation Roleplay world provides a comprehensive overview of various races and their unique characteristics within this fantasy universe. Elves, a nearly extinct and long-lived race, are rarely seen, with the last sighting around 2000 years ago. Beastfolk face harsh challenges, including widespread persecution. Orcs, known for their tribal conflicts, add to the world's dynamic political environment. Drakarians, with their massive size and intelligence, and the magically-created Warforged, contribute to the diversity of this world. Dwarves, with lifespans up to 500 years, offer a contrast to the near-immortal Elves.
=== A Table Of Gaia's Races === {| class="wikitable" ! colspan="2" | === ''<u>'''Races'''</u>'' === |- !Humans !Humans are a versatile and adaptable race known for their ambition, diversity, and capacity for innovation. They come in various ethnicities, and their abilities vary based on individual talents and skills. Humans are known for their resilience, adaptability, and ability to excel in various professions and areas of expertise. Humans lack affinity for magic |- !Dwarves !Dwarves are stout and sturdy beings with a deep affinity for mining, crafting, and underground dwellings. They have a stocky build, remarkable strength, and exceptional craftsmanship skills. Dwarves are renowned for their expertise in forging weapons, armor, and constructing intricate structures. |- !Beastfolk (Minor) !Beastfolk are a diverse race that encompasses various humanoid animal-like beings. They possess characteristics of animals, such as ears, tails, or animalistic features. Beastfolk exhibit traits associated with their animal counterparts, such as enhanced senses, agility, or natural abilities. They often have deep connections to nature and animal companionship, forming bonds with creatures of the wild. |- !Gnomes (Minor) !Gnomes are a diminutive and curious race known for their ingenuity, love of tinkering, and affinity for magic. They have small frames, large heads, and nimble fingers. Gnomes possess exceptional intelligence and often dedicate themselves to the pursuit of knowledge and invention. They are skilled inventors, alchemists, and magicians, crafting intricate devices and harnessing magical energies. |- !Giants (Non-Dominant) !Giants are towering beings known for their immense size and strength. They can vary in appearance, with some resembling colossal humanoids while others embody specific elemental or natural forces. Giants often have long lifespans and possess the ability to manipulate their surroundings. They are often associated with wisdom, guardianship, and the power to shape the landscape. |- !Undead (Non-Dominant) !Undead beings encompass various creatures risen from death or cursed with immortality. They can range from skeletal beings to revenants or vampires, each with distinct characteristics and abilities. Undead often possess dark or necrotic powers, and their presence can evoke fear and unease among other races. They may struggle with their own existence, seeking redemption or embracing their darker nature. |- !Warforged (Non-Dominant) !Warforged are sentient constructs created for warfare and labor. They have a humanoid appearance, but their bodies are made of metal, stone, or other durable materials. Warforged possess enhanced strength, resilience, and the ability to withstand harsh environments. They often have innate magical abilities, and their existence raises questions about identity, free will, and purpose. |- !Nymphs (Non-Dominant) !Nymphs are ethereal beings closely tied to the natural world and its elements. They possess an otherworldly beauty, often adorned with floral or leafy attributes. Nymphs have the ability to manipulate plant life, communicate with animals, and harness nature-based magic. They are guardians of forests, rivers, and other natural sanctuaries, embodying the vitality and grace of nature. |- !Centaurs (Non-Dominant) !Centaurs are hybrid beings with the upper body of a human and the lower body of a horse. They possess exceptional speed, strength, and archery skills. Centaurs are often associated with nature, embodying a harmonious connection between humans and animals. They excel in horsemanship, hunting, and warfare, often revered as skilled warriors. |- !Minotaurs (Non-Dominant) !Minotaurs are powerful humanoid creatures with the head of a bull and the body of a muscular human. They are renowned for their immense strength, endurance, and combat prowess. Minotaurs often excel in melee combat, wielding large weapons with precision. |- !Merfolk (Non-Dominant) !Merfolk are an aquatic race with the upper body of a human and the lower body of a fish or sea creature. They have the ability to breathe underwater, swim with great speed, and communicate with marine life. Merfolk are skilled in water-based magic and are often associated with the mysteries of the ocean. |- !Terranids (Non-Dominant) !Terranids are a race of shapeshifters closely attuned to nature. They have the ability to transform into various animal forms, granting them agility, enhanced senses, and unique abilities associated with each form. Terranids have a deep affinity with the earth, allowing them to communicate with plants and harness the power of nature. Terranids usually have to consume said creature to be able to transform into it. |- !Orcs (Non-Dominant) !Orcs are a robust and formidable race known for their physical strength and fierce warrior culture. They have a muscular build, prominent tusks, and often possess a greenish complexion. Orcs excel in combat and warfare, demonstrating ferocity and tactical prowess on the battlefield. They value strength and honor, and their society is typically organized around powerful chieftains or warlords. |- !Drakarians (Non-Dominant) !Drakarians are a draconic race known for their affinity with fire and immense physical strength. They have scales, sharp claws, and the ability to breathe fire. Drakarians possess exceptional combat skills and resilience, making them formidable warriors. They have a hierarchical society centered around honor and loyalty, with powerful clan structures. |- !High Elves (Non-Dominant) !High Elves are an ancient and graceful race known for their longevity and affinity with nature. They possess pointed ears, slender frames, and often have a deep connection to forests and magic. Elves are skilled marksmen & swordsmen, adept in nature-based magic, and possess heightened agility and perception. White Skinned. |- !Dark Elves (Non-Dominant) !Dark Elves are an ancient and ungraceful race known for their longevity and affinity with the shadows & void, but also their savagery. They possess pointed ears, slender frames, and often have a deep connection to the shadows and magic. Elves are skilled marksmen & swordsmen, adept in shadow-based magic, and possess heightened agility and perception. Dark Skinned. |}

== Prologue "A Wild World" ==
=== Introduction === "Book 0" in the Avant Garde Nation Roleplay world provides a comprehensive overview of various races and their unique characteristics within this fantasy universe. Elves, a nearly extinct and long-lived race, are rarely seen, with the last sighting around 2000 years ago. Beastfolk face harsh challenges, including widespread persecution. Orcs, known for their tribal conflicts, add to the world's dynamic political environment. Drakarians, with their massive size and intelligence, and the magically-created Warforged, contribute to the diversity of this world. Dwarves, with lifespans up to 500 years, offer a contrast to the near-immortal Elves. Warforged are unique beings brought to life by Gnomes using a mystical practice known as Soul Magic. This form of magic involves the caster expending a part of their own health to animate the Warforged, imbuing them with life and consciousness.
=== A Table Of Gaia's Races === {| class="wikitable" ! colspan="2" | === ''<u>'''Races'''</u>'' === |- !Humans !Humans are a versatile and adaptable race known for their ambition, diversity, and capacity for innovation. They come in various ethnicities, and their abilities vary based on individual talents and skills. Humans are known for their resilience, adaptability, and ability to excel in various professions and areas of expertise. Humans lack affinity for magic |- !Dwarves !Dwarves are stout and sturdy beings with a deep affinity for mining, crafting, and underground dwellings. They have a stocky build, remarkable strength, and exceptional craftsmanship skills. Dwarves are renowned for their expertise in forging weapons, armor, and constructing intricate structures. |- !Beastfolk (Minor) !Beastfolk are a diverse race that encompasses various humanoid animal-like beings. They possess characteristics of animals, such as ears, tails, or animalistic features. Beastfolk exhibit traits associated with their animal counterparts, such as enhanced senses, agility, or natural abilities. They often have deep connections to nature and animal companionship, forming bonds with creatures of the wild. |- !Gnomes (Minor) !Gnomes are a diminutive and curious race known for their ingenuity, love of tinkering, and affinity for magic. They have small frames, large heads, and nimble fingers. Gnomes possess exceptional intelligence and often dedicate themselves to the pursuit of knowledge and invention. They are skilled inventors, alchemists, and magicians, crafting intricate devices and harnessing magical energies. |- !Giants (Non-Dominant) !Giants are towering beings known for their immense size and strength. They can vary in appearance, with some resembling colossal humanoids while others embody specific elemental or natural forces. Giants often have long lifespans and possess the ability to manipulate their surroundings. They are often associated with wisdom, guardianship, and the power to shape the landscape. |- !Undead (Non-Dominant) !Undead beings encompass various creatures risen from death or cursed with immortality. They can range from skeletal beings to revenants or vampires, each with distinct characteristics and abilities. Undead often possess dark or necrotic powers, and their presence can evoke fear and unease among other races. They may struggle with their own existence, seeking redemption or embracing their darker nature. |- !Warforged (Non-Dominant) !Warforged are sentient constructs created for warfare and labor. They have a humanoid appearance, but their bodies are made of metal, stone, or other durable materials. Warforged possess enhanced strength, resilience, and the ability to withstand harsh environments. They often have innate magical abilities, and their existence raises questions about identity, free will, and purpose. |- !Nymphs (Non-Dominant) !Nymphs are ethereal beings closely tied to the natural world and its elements. They possess an otherworldly beauty, often adorned with floral or leafy attributes. Nymphs have the ability to manipulate plant life, communicate with animals, and harness nature-based magic. They are guardians of forests, rivers, and other natural sanctuaries, embodying the vitality and grace of nature. |- !Centaurs (Non-Dominant) !Centaurs are hybrid beings with the upper body of a human and the lower body of a horse. They possess exceptional speed, strength, and archery skills. Centaurs are often associated with nature, embodying a harmonious connection between humans and animals. They excel in horsemanship, hunting, and warfare, often revered as skilled warriors. |- !Minotaurs (Non-Dominant) !Minotaurs are powerful humanoid creatures with the head of a bull and the body of a muscular human. They are renowned for their immense strength, endurance, and combat prowess. Minotaurs often excel in melee combat, wielding large weapons with precision. |- !Merfolk (Non-Dominant) !Merfolk are an aquatic race with the upper body of a human and the lower body of a fish or sea creature. They have the ability to breathe underwater, swim with great speed, and communicate with marine life. Merfolk are skilled in water-based magic and are often associated with the mysteries of the ocean. |- !Terranids (Non-Dominant) !Terranids are a race of shapeshifters closely attuned to nature. They have the ability to transform into various animal forms, granting them agility, enhanced senses, and unique abilities associated with each form. Terranids have a deep affinity with the earth, allowing them to communicate with plants and harness the power of nature. Terranids usually have to consume said creature to be able to transform into it. |- !Orcs (Non-Dominant) !Orcs are a robust and formidable race known for their physical strength and fierce warrior culture. They have a muscular build, prominent tusks, and often possess a greenish complexion. Orcs excel in combat and warfare, demonstrating ferocity and tactical prowess on the battlefield. They value strength and honor, and their society is typically organized around powerful chieftains or warlords. |- !Drakarians (Non-Dominant) !Drakarians are a draconic race known for their affinity with fire and immense physical strength. They have scales, sharp claws, and the ability to breathe fire. Drakarians possess exceptional combat skills and resilience, making them formidable warriors. They have a hierarchical society centered around honor and loyalty, with powerful clan structures. |- !High Elves (Non-Dominant) !High Elves are an ancient and graceful race known for their longevity and affinity with nature. They possess pointed ears, slender frames, and often have a deep connection to forests and magic. Elves are skilled marksmen & swordsmen, adept in nature-based magic, and possess heightened agility and perception. White Skinned. |- !Dark Elves (Non-Dominant) !Dark Elves are an ancient and ungraceful race known for their longevity and affinity with the shadows & void, but also their savagery. They possess pointed ears, slender frames, and often have a deep connection to the shadows and magic. Elves are skilled marksmen & swordsmen, adept in shadow-based magic, and possess heightened agility and perception. Dark Skinned. |}

